    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q5",
      "question": "<p>A car has six forward gears.</p><p>The fastest speed of the car</p><ul><li>in 1<sup>st</sup> gear is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"28\\text{ km h}^{-1}\"></span></li><li>in 6<sup>th</sup> gear is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"115\\text{ km h}^{-1}\"></span></li></ul><p>Given that the fastest speed of the car in successive gears is modelled by an <strong>arithmetic sequence</strong>,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find the fastest speed of the car in 3<sup>rd</sup> gear. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the fastest speed of the car in successive gears is modelled by a <strong>geometric sequence</strong>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find the fastest speed of the car in 5<sup>th</sup> gear. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
