    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q6",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin x+2\\cos x\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\\sin(x+\\alpha)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> are constants, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R&gt;0\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\alpha&lt;\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\"></span><br>Give the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> and give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> in radians to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>, inside a room on a given day is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\theta=5+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}-3\\right)+2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}-3\\right)\\qquad 0\\leqslant t&lt;24\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the number of hours after midnight.</p><p>Using the equation of the model and your answer to part (a),</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>deduce the maximum temperature of the room during this day, <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>find the time of day when the maximum temperature occurs, giving your answer to the nearest minute. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
