      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q7",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:85mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q07-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: a U-shaped curve C with minimum point (-2, 13) and a straight line l through (-2, 13) and (0, 25) on the y-axis; the shaded region R lies between l and C for x from -2 to 0.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of a curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> and a straight line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> meets <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> at the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,13)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,25)\"></span> as shown.</p><p>The shaded region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is bounded by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> as shown in Figure 1.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> is a quadratic function in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,13)\"></span> is the minimum turning point of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span></li></ul><p>use inequalities to define <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
