      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q9",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q09-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2: the curve C on axes x and y with origin O; the curve comes down steeply from the upper left, has a minimum just left of the y-axis below the x-axis, rises through the y-axis to a maximum just above the x-axis, then approaches the x-axis from above.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=4\\left(x^2-2\\right)\\mathrm e^{-2x}\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f&#x27;(x)=8\\left(2+x-x^2\\right)\\mathrm e^{-2x}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Hence find, in simplest form, the exact coordinates of the stationary points of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g\"></span> and the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h\"></span> are defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=2\\mathrm f(x)\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h(x)=2\\mathrm f(x)-3\\qquad x\\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the range of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g\"></span></li><li>the range of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
