      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Use the substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=u^2+1\"></span> to show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_5^{10}\\frac{3\\,\\mathrm dx}{(x-1)\\left(3+2\\sqrt{x-1}\\right)}=\\int_p^q\\frac{6\\,\\mathrm du}{u(3+2u)}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are positive constants to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence, using algebraic integration, show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_5^{10}\\frac{3\\,\\mathrm dx}{(x-1)\\left(3+2\\sqrt{x-1}\\right)}=\\ln a\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a rational constant to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
