      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q13",
      "question": "<p>A sequence of numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots\"></span> is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a_{n+1}=\\frac{k\\left(a_n+2\\right)}{a_n}\\qquad n\\in\\mathbb N\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the sequence is a periodic sequence of order 3</li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a_1=2\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k^2+k-2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>For this sequence explain why <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\neq 1\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Find the value of<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{80}a_r\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
