      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2020-october/q14",
      "question": "<p>A large spherical balloon is deflating.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds the balloon has radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\text{ cm}\"></span> and volume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\\text{ cm}^3\"></span></p><p>The volume of the balloon is modelled as decreasing at a constant rate.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Using this model, show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dr}{\\mathrm dt}=-\\frac{k}{r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a positive constant. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the initial radius of the balloon is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\\text{ cm}\"></span></li><li>after 5 seconds the radius of the balloon is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\text{ cm}\"></span></li><li>the volume of the balloon continues to decrease at a constant rate until the balloon is empty</li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>solve the differential equation to find a complete equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Find the limitation on the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> for which the equation in part (b) is valid. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
